      "id": "puppy-4.3.1-multisession",
      "channel": "odd",
      "title": "Puppy Linux 4.3.1: the live CD that saves itself back to the disc",
      "year": 2009,
      "platform": "PC (32-bit x86)",
      "summary": "Puppy loads entirely into RAM, which frees the drive it booted from. At shutdown it can write your session back onto that same disc as a new session, holding only the files that changed. The next boot loads the latest one, until the disc is full.",
      "license": "GPL and other free licences",
      "homepage": "https://bkhome.org/archive/puppylinux/multi-puppy.htm",
      "kind": "disc",
      "boot": "El Torito (BIOS)",
      "burn": {
        "leave_open": true,
        "note": "Burn it with the disc left open for more sessions, or Puppy can't write back to it. DVD-R and DVD+R work best: each CD session wastes about 14 MB. On a rewritable disc, use a full erase to clear it, because a quick erase doesn't remove the old sessions properly."
      },
